# Service tests

Tests live in `service/<feature>_service_test.go`. Mocks: [go-mockery.mdc](./go-mockery.mdc). Errors: [go-errors.mdc](./go-errors.mdc).

## Coverage

Each `internal/<domain>/` must keep **>80%** coverage on `service/` (use `go test -cover ./internal/<domain>/service/...`). Add tests before merging feature work. Update coverage figure in `AGENTS.md` after running tests.

Repository and handler coverage is encouraged; the **80% gate applies to service** unless the project defines otherwise.

## Stack

- `testing`, `testify/assert`, `testify/require`, `testify/mock`
- mockery-generated mocks from `mocks/interfaces`

## Required cases per public service method

| Case | Assert |
|------|--------|
| Success | `assert.NoError`, expected side effects via mock expectations |
| Repository/dependency error | `require.ErrorAs` → `*errors.DomainError` with expected `Code` and `Message` |
| Validation / business branch | No error or specific domain code (duplicate skip, not found, etc.) |

## Pattern

```go
func TestCreate_Success(t *testing.T) {
    repo := mocks.NewMockOrderRepository(t)
    repo.EXPECT().Insert(mock.Anything, mock.Anything).Return(nil)
    svc := NewOrderService(repo)

    err := svc.Create(context.Background(), &models.CreateRequest{ID: "1"})
    assert.NoError(t, err)
}

func TestCreate_RepositoryError(t *testing.T) {
    repo := mocks.NewMockOrderRepository(t)
    repo.EXPECT().Insert(mock.Anything, mock.Anything).Return(assert.AnError)
    svc := NewOrderService(repo)

    err := svc.Create(context.Background(), &models.CreateRequest{ID: "1"})
    var domainErr *errors.DomainError
    require.ErrorAs(t, err, &domainErr)
    assert.Equal(t, errors.CodeInternal, domainErr.Code)
}
```

## Conventions

- Table-driven tests when ≥3 input variants
- `t.Helper()` on shared builders
- One logical behavior per `Test*` function
- No real DB or HTTP in service tests
- Test package `service` (same package) unless project uses `service_test`

## When to add tests

- New or changed service method with any branch
- Bug fix: regression test first
- Pure delegation with zero branches: minimal test optional; still keep package above 80% overall

## Avoid

- Testing handlers or SQL here
- Global state between tests
- Sleep/time-based flakiness
- Asserting on log output unless project standard requires it
